  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\n   We improve upon the previous implementation by introducing a hybrid optimization strategy that combines global exploration with localized refinement. The key bottleneck addressed is the susceptibility to local optima in the SLSQP solver used in the original implementation. \n\n   We introduce:\n   - Temperature-scheduled evolutionary phase using dual_annealing to escape local optima\n   - Progressive refinement through local non-linear optimization\n   - Multi-resolution exploration by strategically increasing resolution levels\n   - Adaptive seeding of perturbations based on convergence patterns\n   - Linear-constraint projection mechanism ensuring valid candidates throughout the search\n\n2. Mathematical specification\n   - Objective optimization: minimize C5 = max_k \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx\n   - Constraint enforcement: 0 <= h[x] <= 1, \u222bh[x]dx = 1\n   - Resolution adaptation: candidate solutions start at lower resolutions (n=90) then escalate to final resolution (n=180)\n   - Projection operator: L2 projection constrained by problem conditions\n\n3. Implementation procedure\n   - Phase initialization:\n     h0 = initial_h_values.copy() if provided else generate_initial_candidate()\n     n = 180 points, target_integral = 90.0\n   - Global exploration (20% budget):\n     For each of 3 seeds:\n        Perform dual_annealing with random mutations\n        Track elite candidates by projected descent\n   - Progressive refinement (40% budget):\n     Three-tier optimization:\n        1. Constrained with analytic gradient for max-overlap penalty\n        2. Smooth penalty schedule with temperature reduction\n        3. Adaptable line-search local optimization\n   - Resolution escalation (30% budget):\n     Increase resolution to 360 points\n     Apply multi-frequency smoothing\n     Perform localized minima search\n   - Final cleanup (rest of budget):\n     Apply hard clipping and re-projection\n   - Fitness selection: candidates validated by exact overlap integral comparison\n\n4. Search choices and variations\n   - Initial seeds: random Gaussian perturbations (variance=0.1)\n   - Global moves: Cauchy-distributed mutations\n   - Refinement stages: adaptive to elapsed wall time\n   - Resolution upgrade: triggered when perturbation isolation exceeds threshold\n   - Mutation spectrum: temperature-dependent (0.01 to 0.001)\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n   - Global phase: 20% of 1100s \u2248 220s\n   - Refinement phase: 40% of 1100s \u2248 440s\n   - Resolution upgrade: 30% of 1100s \u2248 330s\n   - Timeout handling: autosave best candidate at any failure\n   - Repair mechanism: linear projection with threshold \u03b5=1e-5\n   - Robustness margin: constrained optimization attempts\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n   - Final candidate must pass: 0<=h[i]<=1 and np.sum(h)*dx\u22481\n   - Calculation: dx=2/len(h); integral = np.sum(h)*dx\n   - Objective verification: np.max(np.correlate(h,1-h,mode='full')*dx)\n   - Format validation: 3-element return (h_array, objective, len(h_array))\n   - Convergence monitoring: time-normalized improvement tracks",
